+Attacks. The panel includes mean-closeness outliers, largest-fit greedy,
+uniform restarts, a nearest-average single-swap ansatz, a Lagarias-Odlyzko-style
+fixed-cardinality lattice embedding with bounded LLL, and exact cardinality
+branch-and-bound. Difficulty grows by adding ordinary rows while k and the
+answer length stay fixed.
 
+Canonicalization. Any permutation of ordinary rows, with the witness carried
+through it and the control kept last, preserves Appendix B.1's problem.
+canonical_key sorts the distinct encoded weights and keeps the target, k and
+hyperparameters. It is complete for that row-permutation symmetry, but not for
+more general affine equivalences between unrelated subset-sum encodings.
