codex
Built and locally verified the Track B generator based on Theorem 4.4 / Appendix B.1 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.01365).

Key results:

- G1–G9(c) pass locally.
- Exact shipping density: 600 / 68,923,264,410.
- Random guesses: 0 / 200,000.
- Five attacks: 0 / 8 successes each.
- Reference meet-in-the-middle: 1,572,864 states, 3,145,725 operations, 20.09 seconds.
- Compact residue decomposition: at most 180 operations.
- Answer: 20 IDs, 72 characters.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.01365/gen_2408_01365.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.01365/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.01365/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.01365/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.01365/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2408.01365/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The only unresolved requirement is oracle hardening: all twelve OpenRouter requests returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” before inference. The transcripts preserve those script-generated errors, but they do not establish a `hardened` verdict. The paper has therefore not been rejected; the artifact is marked locally verified and awaiting restored OpenRouter quota.
